    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands as the unequivocal anchor of our lineup with an elite 85.94 score. His matchup against Lorenzen is perfectly set up for production, buoyed by a significant park factor (+14%) and a favorable batting order position that maximizes his potential for both counting stats and stolen base opportunities. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.50) also project as high-ceiling plays, particularly due to their top-of-the-order usage and advantageous platoons against their respective starters. **Brice Turang** remains a high-priority start at 70.33; beyond his solid base projection, his efficiency is boosted by an 87% stolen base success rate against the starter's slow delivery, making him a critical weapon for our scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who posted a 44.89 score against Soroka. While the park conditions in that matchup provided a +14% boost, **Karros** ultimately missed the cut because the density of high-efficiency bats in our primary lineup\u2014specifically the power-focused profiles of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Josh Naylor**\u2014offered a higher collective probability for RBI and HR contributions. We are keeping **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story** stashed on the IL, though their absence continues to pinch our depth for stolen base specialists. \n\nInvestors should note the minor risk flag on **Brice Turang**, where inward-blowing wind has shaved 5% off his raw projection, though his SB utility outweighs this volatility. Conversely, **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a strong start at 72.92, benefiting from a rare combination of wind blowing out and a positive platoon edge. With **Dalton Rushing** and **Gabriel Moreno** both active, we have redundancy at catcher, but today's matchups warrant deploying both to capitalize on the favorable SP xERAs we are targeting across the board. We remain diligent on the status of **Max Muncy**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Carson Williams**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte**, who remain ready for rotation as the 2026 campaign progresses.",
